	(text "EA_FILT: Filtered channel A at the Schmitt input 1A; ${533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2:REFERENCE} and ${6d1535c2-80f9-4b43-98b1-667f7a6325c8:REFERENCE} form the 72 kHz corner." (at 423.76 167.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "12677861-18fb-5d45-9968-b575647e58e9"))
	(text "EB_FILT: Filtered channel B at the Schmitt input 2A; ${9c095d77-bc49-4401-aec8-d7ddc8bd052d:REFERENCE} and ${a305d72b-1111-4933-8025-f63ece306fdf:REFERENCE} form the 72 kHz corner." (at 423.76 171.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "55355b16-9cc8-5004-88f2-3dab6b0b8059"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 183.22) (xy 578.76 183.22)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "cc0a37cc-4a5a-5873-9210-216ba26cf66c"))
	(text "OPERATION" (at 423.76 185.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "62e1f04f-0a78-5a61-b06f-9273d92d24f9"))
	(text "Signal path per channel: EA -> ${533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2:REFERENCE} (4.7 k) -> EA_FILT -> ${cf752abf-0e0c-412d-a73f-c1eaff636f88:REFERENCE} 1A (pin 1) -> 1Y (pin 6) = ENCA; EB -> ${9c095d77-bc49-4401-aec8-d7ddc8bd052d:REFERENCE} -> EB_FILT -> 2A" (at 423.76 189.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "66090bb9-ae1a-5e0f-a1b2-9fa413b17a83"))
	(text "(pin 3) -> 2Y (pin 4) = ENCB. A/B only: an index channel needs a second buffer." (at 423.76 192.45 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "db4b8825-e4a7-5b92-b46c-58731998d8c8"))
	(text "Each series resistor with its 470 pF shunt (${6d1535c2-80f9-4b43-98b1-667f7a6325c8:REFERENCE}, ${a305d72b-1111-4933-8025-f63ece306fdf:REFERENCE}) is a low-pass of tau = 4.7 k x 470 pF = 2.2 us, corner about 72 kHz; it removes" (at 423.76 196.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ea27dd28-3a09-5ef7-9535-bbab3f611d25"))
	(text "harness noise and slows the edge into a Schmitt input, which has no slew-rate limit." (at 423.76 198.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f523a94d-1ded-5959-b93d-4b08a0c13633"))
	(text "${cf752abf-0e0c-412d-a73f-c1eaff636f88:REFERENCE} (SN74LVC2G17, 1.65 to 5.5 V supply) at 3.3 V: VT+ 1.3 to 2.0 V, VT- 0.8 to 1.3 V (facts at 3 V), 0.4 V minimum hysteresis; inputs are 5.5 V" (at 423.76 202.61 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a7abb8ce-85ce-50fa-aee5-e250a4f93843"))
	(text "tolerant with no clamp to VCC, so the 5 V encoder drives them directly and Ioff (10 uA max) keeps the outputs high-impedance when +3.3V is down." (at 423.76 205.15 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a59fd5bf-eac8-5e07-88ab-c84b6b81d56d"))
	(text "${533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2:REFERENCE} and ${9c095d77-bc49-4401-aec8-d7ddc8bd052d:REFERENCE} are also the protection: a harness short to a 36 V rail is bounded to about 7.7 mA. ${79c28129-1db5-4228-b75d-5e0c7ecd3466:REFERENCE} and ${fcea27a1-25e8-4535-8db3-33361bde811c:REFERENCE} (100 k) define the" (at 423.76 208.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "72753316-955f-5972-8572-36b29db16562"))
	(text "inputs when the harness is unplugged; ${e69b9f00-5592-4480-9192-6b0f166869f7:REFERENCE} and ${3347de5d-a753-454e-ab35-f4f87e410fba:REFERENCE} (100 k) hold ENCA and ENCB low when the buffer is unpowered, so a downstream" (at 423.76 211.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b4f1fce5-615f-5e1f-82cd-63be0cf5e590"))
	(text "instrument never sees a floating input." (at 423.76 214.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "43beb767-0a58-5cb9-979b-3dc7d9706119"))
	(text "${67e9b657-6e21-4eed-a291-0f4764823597:REFERENCE} and ${94d002ab-253a-4bf8-a1f5-06c9a55848cc:REFERENCE} (100 ohm) are the instrument taps to ENCA_INST and ENCB_INST (convention 14: the block owns its outputs). ${14506acd-770d-4602-a934-c96be3627a02:REFERENCE} (4.7 uF)" (at 423.76 217.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4e34fd39-9fd4-5b40-8135-6a8881027996"))
	(text "and ${e649e3cc-8b13-473b-b687-a057c945920c:REFERENCE} (100 nF) bypass the encoder supply VENC near the harness; ${27b1961b-dbb5-447e-98d1-8ba97d676414:REFERENCE} (100 nF) bypasses VCC at pin 5." (at 423.76 220.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e36d9086-a00d-53c5-8658-3cf63dce451b"))
	(text "The placing board provides VENC and +3.3V from the same switched domain as the encoder consumer, the GND return and the harness connector; it" (at 423.76 224.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3e7b7f5c-bc19-5b68-8e54-222611b22e4d"))
	(text "decides ENCN handling when no index channel exists." (at 423.76 226.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3dfd8f15-59ba-5b42-87a8-a4c9ad528a1d"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 238.17) (xy 578.76 238.17)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "82365e43-71dc-58b3-9a8f-caf05a353981"))
	(text "DESIGN CONTRACT" (at 423.76 240.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a6f37866-f1e5-52eb-835e-42a722a956fc"))
	(text "Single-ended 5 V quadrature encoder input: per-channel series/RC conditioning plus an SN74LVC2G17 dual Schmitt-trigger buffer that translates an" (at 423.76 244.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d9303d24-1b3a-5c76-9bc2-99051e91cb5b"))
	(text "encoder's 5 V push-pull A/B outputs into clean 3.3 V logic. The connector deliberately lives outside the block, the same way" (at 423.76 247.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f3575dc0-403f-5884-b5e7-e93c3873a0cb"))
	(text "differential_encoder_receiver is built, so one block serves screw-terminal, IDC, JST or Molex harnesses and the parent picks the housing to suit the" (at 423.76 249.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a1d8537c-6a23-50c6-8aaa-af5e526c527d"))
	(text "machine. Bring the raw encoder channels in on EA and EB and take conditioned logic out on ENCA and ENCB; ENCA_INST and ENCB_INST are their" (at 423.76 252.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8ceca711-6db1-530d-95d4-766d2949c860"))
	(text "instrument taps. Use this for TTL/push-pull encoders; use differential_encoder_receiver instead for RS-422 A+/A-/B+/B- encoders." (at 423.76 255.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7bcab14d-3b6b-542e-8058-d91e21ce5439"))
	(text "The Schmitt input is the point of the block: a typical 5 V encoder rises in about 100 ns over a 4 V swing, roughly 25 ns/V, which violates the 8 ns/V" (at 423.76 257.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "dc26c26f-423a-5195-ad88-d4566e494e6e"))
	(text "input transition rate limit of an ordinary LVC buffer and would let noise on the slow edge double-clock the quadrature counter into permanent, silent" (at 423.76 260.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d746e3ba-6f51-5074-8e1b-abedaa03d910"))
	(text "position error. The 2G17 has no such limit and 0.4 V minimum hysteresis at 3 V, and it closes against the encoder's guaranteed worst case with 400" (at 423.76 262.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6ca5a237-20d5-550f-abcc-fc0b6ab03845"))
	(text "mV to spare on both rails: VOH >= 2.4 V versus VT+ <= 2.0 V, VOL <= 0.4 V versus VT- >= 0.8 V. Do not substitute a resistive divider into a 3.3 V" (at 423.76 265.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "69d30ae4-abbe-566b-af49-b1a751389285"))
	(text "input: dividing the encoder's guaranteed 2.4 V VOH by 0.66 gives 1.58 V, below the 2.31 V VINHI of a 3.3 V VCC_IO TMC5130A input, and loading the" (at 423.76 267.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9d074573-5e45-5619-a483-dfe3901dd874"))
	(text "output makes it worse." (at 423.76 270.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e057b3d8-f102-55aa-8f55-3afc27e8565c"))
	(text "The 4.7 kohm series resistors ${533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2:REFERENCE}/${9c095d77-bc49-4401-aec8-d7ddc8bd052d:REFERENCE} are the protection element and the reason the block tolerates a field-wired harness: they bound a" (at 423.76 272.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e988e766-178c-5d43-ae14-349f53622337"))
	(text "short to a 36 V rail to about 7 mA, so a miswire kills a 0.19 USD buffer instead of the motor driver. The 100 kohm resistors ${79c28129-1db5-4228-b75d-5e0c7ecd3466:REFERENCE}/${fcea27a1-25e8-4535-8db3-33361bde811c:REFERENCE} sit" (at 423.76 275.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d12b23ad-9c19-5385-846f-26efcc972a7f"))
	(text "on the harness side of those series resistors rather than after them, so they define the buffer input when the harness is unplugged without forming a" (at 423.76 277.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "922faa87-17fd-53a2-9b58-e2010153b9cb"))
	(text "divider that would eat VIH margin; ${e69b9f00-5592-4480-9192-6b0f166869f7:REFERENCE}/${3347de5d-a753-454e-ab35-f4f87e410fba:REFERENCE} on the outputs cover Ioff high-Z when the buffer's supply is down, so an always-on downstream" (at 423.76 280.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "66fba345-b52f-5c0c-b188-ced8f43c89b2"))
	(text "instrumentation buffer never sees a floating input." (at 423.76 282.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "74e1bd0b-4641-5865-b051-faa2d770736c"))
	(text "The VENC and +3.3V ports are intentionally generic so a parent can bind them to whatever it calls its rails, but the electrical requirement is not" (at 423.76 285.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9bf5144c-176c-5652-a3d4-bd21111ffd3b"))
	(text "generic: on any board where the encoder's consumer can be powered down, bind both to that board's SWITCHED domain, so the encoder, this buffer" (at 423.76 288.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e59e6125-5f4b-581c-93a4-81b48b14ae3c"))
	(text "and the consumer rise and fall together. Rail sequencing between the two is a non-issue: inputs are rated 0 to 5.5 V at any valid VCC with 6.5 V" (at 423.76 290.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9439ee6e-f3f5-5c8f-a2f5-6f27fc59a594"))
	(text "absolute maximum and no clamp diode to VCC, and Ioff disables the outputs when the part is unpowered." (at 423.76 293.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "818aea1b-d814-509d-a12f-9ea4ba8ae793"))
	(text "Size ${6d1535c2-80f9-4b43-98b1-667f7a6325c8:REFERENCE}/${a305d72b-1111-4933-8025-f63ece306fdf:REFERENCE} for a corner >= 10x CPR*RPM/60; 27 pF gives 1.25 MHz, 470 pF gives 72 kHz for a slow axis that needs more rejection." (at 423.76 295.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "38e68c70-5d75-5b29-9627-31a0969d9ebf"))
	(text "This block covers A/B only. If your encoder has an index channel, add a second SN74LVC2G17 with its spare input tied to GND; if it does not, the" (at 423.76 298.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "217dcdab-a4d7-53ea-89d8-7f3a3b993c1a"))
	(text "consuming controller's index pin still needs an explicit tie: the TMC5130A datasheet requires ENCN be pulled to GND or VCC_IO when unused." (at 423.76 300.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cc2f1a02-0525-57ba-938d-c669ed2739b5"))
	(text "For layout: ${14506acd-770d-4602-a934-c96be3627a02:REFERENCE} and ${e649e3cc-8b13-473b-b687-a057c945920c:REFERENCE} decouple the encoder supply VENC and want to sit as close to the parent's encoder connector as placement allows;" (at 423.76 303.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ed27aa7b-f433-5b89-aa00-26937252e047"))
	(text "${533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2:REFERENCE} and ${9c095d77-bc49-4401-aec8-d7ddc8bd052d:REFERENCE} at the block's input edge, ${6d1535c2-80f9-4b43-98b1-667f7a6325c8:REFERENCE} at ${cf752abf-0e0c-412d-a73f-c1eaff636f88:REFERENCE} pin 1 and ${a305d72b-1111-4933-8025-f63ece306fdf:REFERENCE} at pin 3 with short returns; ${27b1961b-dbb5-447e-98d1-8ba97d676414:REFERENCE} hard against" (at 423.76 305.82 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a808a041-059f-5978-855a-1d9374435eb2"))
	(text "${fdd2edbd-24fa-460f-8e8d-56e4d4752cb6:REFERENCE} pin 5; route the A/B pair with a ground reference between them and well away from motor bridge outputs." (at 423.76 308.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f8e3b471-87c4-57ee-9e6d-cb399a141307"))
	(group "Review page 01: 1. Channel A input conditioning" (uuid "b3653c1b-d757-5d04-98a1-1df34d4429f3") (members "79c28129-1db5-4228-b75d-5e0c7ecd3466" "05f83307-51b1-54de-9639-2c635d1668f3" "1d5ea1c0-fa37-5b1b-9af9-0739759406fc" "09176c32-c230-591d-a781-ebf08da5a758" "83cdf92f-b576-50a3-a031-fd1d72a405b7" "533278ea-d0f9-4c1e-a477-91c96b62a9c2" "a2439cdd-12ef-5311-ab60-75240d9cbc1a" "afe4a02e-cbca-5d3f-8d8b-5cad402e6da8" "fefc4927-2a1e-5b81-bd36-1b9ef62cde09" "ba781eb0-b298-5c97-959e-5039faee46c9" "dbc3fea1-8444-5c65-bb04-3a557cc5741d" "2d62b8bc-ccd3-5341-996b-0a073f686c61" "07a960b7-2498-5170-b587-8cad341315b5" "90ed9ebb-9093-58d9-892b-d69df0a81d18" "c2e138c1-4cef-58e9-8475-01c13a1c9f6b" "151058f1-63e2-50eb-be2b-a0e2fb92237f" "a24de7b0-5b5e-5062-897b-f5ffebfbb823" "fb5c02ee-d6f4-551e-92ab-1570566e845e" "c1bf8234-4da0-5e6b-9f44-96ec755ebbf5" "ae88b655-fbc4-50a5-89b8-f171b8b410ef" "4e13d5f9-6159-5d87-bd25-9174b8c558c1"))
